Pseudo-code:
```typescript
class ExtractionLogger {
  private startTime: number;

  logStageStart(stage: string) {
    if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development') {
      console.log(`[Extraction] ${stage} started`);
      this.startTime = Date.now();
    }
  }

  logStageEnd(stage: string) {
    if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development') {
      const duration = Date.now() - this.startTime;
      console.log(`[Extraction] ${stage} completed in ${duration}ms`);
    }
  }

  logRetryAttempt(attempt: number, maxAttempts: number) {
    console.log(`[Extraction] Retrying (attempt ${attempt} of ${maxAttempts})...`);
  }
}
```

1. Create `src/lib/extraction/retry-handler.ts` with retry wrapper function
2. Implement exponential backoff: 1s, 2s, 4s between attempts
3. Maximum 3 attempts total
4. Only retry transient errors (FETCH_ERROR, TIMEOUT_ERROR, PARSE_ERROR)
5. Don't retry permanent errors (INVALID_URL)
6. Add cancellation support for user interruption

Pseudo-code:
```typescript
interface RetryConfig {
  maxAttempts: number;
  baseDelay: number;
  retryableErrors: ErrorType[];
}

async function withRetry<T>(
  operation: () => Promise<T>,
  config: RetryConfig,
  logger: ExtractionLogger
): Promise<T> {
  let lastError: ExtractionError;

  for (let attempt = 1; attempt <= config.maxAttempts; attempt++) {
    try {
      return await operation();
    } catch (error) {
      lastError = error;

      if (!config.retryableErrors.includes(error.type) || attempt === config.maxAttempts) {
        throw error;
      }

      const delay = config.baseDelay * Math.pow(2, attempt - 1) * 1000;
      logger.logRetryAttempt(attempt + 1, config.maxAttempts);
      await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, delay));
    }
  }

  throw lastError;
}
```

1. Create array of fallback selectors in order of preference
2. Try `#content.content` (current), then `#content`, then `article`
3. Return content from first successful selector
4. Log which selector worked for debugging
5. Modify existing parse logic to use fallback strategy

Pseudo-code:
```typescript
const FALLBACK_SELECTORS = [
  '#content.content',
  '#content', 
  'article',
  '.article-content',
  'main'
];

function parseContentWithFallback(html: string, logger: ExtractionLogger): string {
  const $ = cheerio.load(html);

  for (const selector of FALLBACK_SELECTORS) {
    const content = $(selector).html();
    if (content && content.trim()) {
      logger.logStageEnd(`Parse (using ${selector})`);
      return content;
    }
  }

  throw new ExtractionError({
    type: ErrorType.PARSE_ERROR,
    message: 'No content found with any fallback selector',
    stage: 'parse'
  });
}
```

